367, 48.414, 48.46, 48.518, 48.6, 48.669, 48.727, 48.762, 48.808, 48.936, 48.983, 49.145, 49.215, 49.377, 49.459, 49.552, 49.575, 49.749, 49.807, 49.842, 49.888, 49.935, 50.051, 50.167, 50.376, 50.515, 50.585, 50.631, 50.655, 50.713, 50.736, 50.794, 50.829, 50.887, 50.933, 50.968, 50.991, 51.015, 51.073, 51.131, 51.235, 51.305, 51.374, 51.421, 51.479, 51.595, 51.792, 52.222, 52.268, 52.303, 52.361, 52.396, 52.489, 52.535, 52.64, 52.721, 52.791, 52.861, 52.895, 52.953, 53.011, 53.093, 53.151, 53.22, 53.278, 53.429, 53.604, 53.963]}, "text": "The brothers need someone to live in it.\n\nAlong the shore they find two fallen trees.\n\nThey shape them into the first man and woman, Ask and Embla.\n\nOdin gives them breath, and their world is called Midgard, the middle world.\n\nAbove it, the gods build their own home, Asgard, and join the two with a rainbow bridge.\n\nHolding everything together is an enormous ash tree, Iggdrasil.\n\nIts roots run down to the gods, the frost giants, and the dead.\n\nAn eagle sits at the top.\n\nA dragon gnaws at the bottom.\n\nAnd a squirrel runs between them, carrying insults.\n\nAt the well of Meemir, Odin trades one eye for a drink.\n\nThat is why Odin has one eye, a wide hat, and a lot of secrets.\n\nThen Loki walks in."}